","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T12:38:39Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T12:38:39Z","body":"Closing in favor of #111162\r\nAs mentioned above, side menu is not compatible with native file dialogs (i.e. dialogs managed by the operating system). On some platforms native dialogs are the only available file dialogs, so this feature effectively causes platform disparity.\r\n\r\nFor advanced file options, you should either use the options provided by FileDialog (compatible with native dialogs), or show a config dialog after selecting the file (like some apps do). Blender is an exception here; I actually wonder how it works in sandboxed environments.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426396667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]